{
  "name": "cxx-qt",
  "description": "CXX-Qt is a language interoperability framework that extends the CXX bridge to provide bidirectional bindings between Rust and C++ specifically for the Qt ecosystem. It utilizes procedural macros and code generation to implement QObject subclasses in Rust, enabling seamless integration with Qt's signal-slot mechanism, property system, and QML runtimes. The project facilitates the embedding of Rust logic into CMake-based C++ applications and allows for the construction of standalone Rust applications with deep Qt integration.",
